\"lists\".\"id\" AS \"lists_id\", \"lists\".\"name\" AS \"lists_name\", \"lists\".\"owner\" AS \"lists_owner\" FROM \"shopping_list\" \"lists\" INNER JOIN \"user\" \"User\" ON \"User\".\"id\"=\"lists\".\"owner\" WHERE \"user\".\"id\"=$1 -- PARAMETERS: [1]`\r\n\r\nIf I don't lazy load and use add the join to the repo.findById (everything works fine)[https://github.com/ericwooley/graphql-typeorm-passport-boilerplate/blob/master/src/graphql/queries/user.ts#L6]\r\n\r\n```\r\nconst user = await userRepo.findOneById(request.user.id, {\r\n      alias: 'user',\r\n      innerJoinAndSelect: {\r\n        \"lists\": \"user.lists\"\r\n    }\r\n})\r\n```\r\n\r\nI have a [user](https://github.com/ericwooley/graphql-typeorm-passport-boilerplate/blob/master/src/models/user.ts#L26) class, with a lazy loaded one to many relationship: \r\n```\r\n@Table()\r\nexport default class User {\r\n\t// ...\r\n\t@OneToMany(type => ShoppingList, shoppingList => shoppingList.owner, {\r\n\t\tcascadeAll: true\r\n\t})\r\n\tlists: Promise<ShoppingList[]>\r\n        // ... \r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nand a class for [ShoppingList](https://github.com/ericwooley/graphql-typeorm-passport-boilerplate/blob/master/src/models/shoppingList.ts)\r\n```\r\n@Table()\r\n       // ...\r\n\t@ManyToOne(type => User, user => user.lists, {\r\n\t\tcascadeAll: true,\r\n\t})\r\n\towner: Promise<User>\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nI cannot figure out for the life of me, why this where clause is being added. Maybe it's something dumb I am doing, but I have tried messing with it every way I can think of. ","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/typeorm/typeorm/issues/234/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/typeorm/typeorm/issues/234/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"id":936860351,"node_id":"MDE0Ok1lbnRpb25lZEV2ZW50OTM2ODYwMzUx","url":"https://api.github.com